      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Common arguments against high-density development often center on the strain it will put on local infrastructure, like traffic, water, and public services.  NIMBY (Not In My Back Yard) opposition frequently focuses on the perceived \"loss of neighborhood character\" and the potential for increased \"overcrowding\" in the immediate area.\n\nSkeptics may also argue that high-rise construction will negatively impact the view-shed and the local \"feel\" of the community, sometimes leading to concerns about the loss of green space.",
