      "content": "ok, so it's more about the \"political divide\" i get that. but if you're looking at it from a professional urban planning perspective, isn't the consensus basically that high density is the only way to solve housing shortages and environmental issues? it feels like the opposition is always just trying to block progress that's objectively better for the city in the long run.",
